---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// The Official Rules, /giveaway/rules. This is the DRAFT wording from the
// Copy table of the plan "Publish the giveaway's Official Rules"
//, word for word. Per that task and "Build
// the Official Rules page", this wording must
// be reviewed by a lawyer licensed in Nevada and approved before October 1,
// 2026 — see "Finalize the Official Rules wording".
// The visible banner below marks this as a draft; delete the <div
// data-draft-banner> block (and its <style>) once the approved wording
// replaces this file's text and "Last updated" is set to the approval date.
//
// The page uses no script and calls no API, matching the task's
// specification, so it works with JavaScript off and needs no offline
// handling of its own.
const title = 'Official Rules · Week Without Driving Las Vegas';
const description =
  'The Official Rules for the Week Without Driving Las Vegas Giveaway, October 1 to 8, 2026.';
const lastUpdated = 'September 22, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description}>
  <section class="container-page container-prose py-12 md:py-16">
    <div data-draft-banner class="draft-banner">
      <strong>Draft: final wording pending review.</strong> This page shows draft rules that have not
      yet been reviewed by a lawyer licensed in Nevada or approved. Do not rely on this wording for an
      actual entry until it is finalized.
    </div>

    <h1 class="text-display-sm">Official Rules</h1>
    <p class="lede mt-2">Week Without Driving Las Vegas Giveaway, October 1 to 8, 2026</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-on-surface-variant">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="prose-doc mt-10">
      <h2>1. Who runs the giveaway</h2>
      <p>
        The Week Without Driving Las Vegas Giveaway (the giveaway) is run by Las Vegans for Better
        Transit (LVBT), a volunteer transit advocacy group in Las Vegas, Nevada.
      </p>

      <h2>2. No purchase or post necessary</h2>
      <p>
        No purchase or post necessary. Buying something or posting on social media does not improve
        your chances of winning. The free entry in section 5 has the same chance as every other
        entry. Joining LVBT's newsletter does not affect your chances of winning.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Who can enter</h2>
      <p>
        You can enter if you live in Southern Nevada (Clark, Esmeralda, Lincoln or Nye County,
        Nevada) and are 13 or older when you enter. If you are 13 to 17, your parent or guardian
        must agree to these rules before you enter. People who can sign in to the giveaway's
        volunteer pages, and anyone else who helps run the giveaway, cannot win. The giveaway is
        void where the law does not allow it.
      </p>

      <h2>4. When</h2>
      <p>
        The giveaway runs from 12:00 am on October 1, 2026 to 11:59 pm on October 8, 2026, Las Vegas
        time (Pacific Daylight Time). Each day runs from midnight to midnight, Las Vegas time.
      </p>

      <h2>5. How to enter</h2>
      <p>There are three ways to enter. Each gives the same one entry for the day.</p>
      <p>
        Upload: on lvwwd.org/giveaway, type your Instagram handle, answer the age question, and
        upload a screenshot or photo of something you did without driving that day.
      </p>
      <p>
        Instagram tag: post a photo, reel or story about something you did without driving that day
        and tag @lasvegasfortransit. If your account is private, also send the post or story to
        @lasvegasfortransit by direct message the same day. Volunteers count tags by hand, and a tag
        counts for the day it was posted.
      </p>
      <p>
        Free entry: on lvwwd.org/giveaway, type your email address or US phone number and answer the
        age question. You do not need to upload, post or buy anything. If you can't use the form,
        email wwd@lasvegasfortransit.org with the subject Giveaway entry, and a volunteer enters
        your email address for the day your email arrives.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are 13 to 17, tick the box saying your parent or guardian agrees to these rules on
        the upload or free entry form. For Instagram tags, send @lasvegasfortransit a direct message
        that says: I'm 13 to 17 and my parent or guardian agrees to the Official Rules.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Limits</h2>
      <p>
        You can get one entry a day and at most 8 entries in total. Entering more than one way on
        the same day still counts as one entry. Use one way to identify yourself for the whole
        giveaway: one Instagram handle, one email address, or one phone number. Entries from a
        person who uses more than one to get more than one entry a day, and entries made by
        automated means, are removed from the draw.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Prize</h2>
      <p>
        There is one prize: a one-month (30-day) RTC bus pass and an LVBT sticker pack. RTC is the
        Regional Transportation Commission of Southern Nevada. The approximate retail value is $75:
        $65 for the pass and $10 for the sticker pack. The winner chooses the pass in the rideRTC
        app or as a pass that doesn't need a phone. The prize cannot be exchanged for cash. Because
        the prize is worth less than $600, LVBT does not collect a tax form from the winner.
      </p>

      <h2>8. How the winner is chosen</h2>
      <p>
        LVBT draws one winner at random from all eligible entries by October 15, 2026. Each entry is
        one chance, so your odds depend on how many entries you have and how many entries there are
        in total.
      </p>

      <h2>9. How the winner is contacted</h2>
      <p>
        LVBT contacts the winner the way they entered: by Instagram direct message from
        @lasvegasfortransit, by email from wwd@lasvegasfortransit.org, or by text message from
        LVBT's Week Without Driving number. The winner has 7 days from that message to reply. If the
        winner does not reply within 7 days, or cannot accept the prize under these rules, LVBT
        draws a new winner the same way. LVBT never asks for money, passwords or bank details.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Winners under 18</h2>
      <p>
        If the winner is 13 to 17, the prize is awarded in the name of their parent or guardian, who
        signs the winner release in section 11 before the prize is handed over or mailed.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Winner release</h2>
      <p>
        Before receiving the prize, the winner signs this release. If the winner is under 18, their
        parent or guardian signs it. It can be signed on paper when the prize is handed over, or by
        replying to LVBT's message with the words I agree to the winner release, followed by the
        signer's full name.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        <p>
          I confirm that the winner lives in Southern Nevada, was 13 or older when they entered, and
          does not help run the giveaway. I accept the prize under the Official Rules. If the winner
          is under 18, I am their parent or guardian, and I accept the prize in my name for them. I
          agree, or I do not agree, that LVBT may share the winner's first name and neighborhood on
          its website and social media.
        </p>
      </blockquote>

      <h2>12. Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        LVBT uses Instagram handles, email addresses, phone numbers and screenshots only to run the
        giveaway, and deletes them on November 30, 2026. Read our <a href="/privacy">Privacy page</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Instagram</h2>
      <p>
        This promotion is not sponsored, endorsed, administered by, or associated with Instagram. By
        entering, you agree that Instagram is not responsible for the giveaway in any way, and you
        release Instagram from any claim about it.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Questions</h2>
      <p>Email wwd@lasvegasfortransit.org.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10">
      <a href="/giveaway" class="body-link font-semibold">&#8592; Back to the giveaway</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .draft-banner {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    border: 2px solid var(--color-primary);
    background: var(--color-primary-container, var(--color-surface-container));
    color: var(--color-primary-ink);
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    font-size: var(--text-body-sm);
  }
</style>
